WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.589
It's been 20 years since The Matrix changed
genre cinema forever.

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:08.770
And now, Lana Wachowski, Keanu Reeves, and
Carrie-Anne Moss are returning for a fourth

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:09.770
film.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.520
So we’re taking a look at some of the biggest
questions we want answered in The Matrix 4.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.840
Now that we know Keanu Reeves is returning
for more of The Matrix, the big question is

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.840
how his character, Neo, comes back after his
apparent death in The Matrix Revolutions.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.080
The Oracle suggests we might see him again
at the end of the last film...

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.160
"Will we ever see him again?"

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.320
"I suspect so.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.280
Someday."

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.970
...but his body is carried away by the Machines
after he defeats Agent Smith and reboots the

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:38.970
Matrix.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.390
There are a number of ways the film could
explain Neo's return, the most obvious of

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.850
which is by telling us he didn't really die
after all, and that the Machines ultimately

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.399
nursed him back to health.

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:51.880
Then there's the explanation that because
of his status as "the One," Neo was always

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:57.170
at least partially a software creation, the
product of programming mixing with biology.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:01.110
Perhaps the software in him survived and reincarnated
into the new Matrix.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.840
Whatever the case, we can't wait to see how
we get him back.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.400
"Yeah, I'm thinkin' I'm back!"

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.990
Neo is the One, so there are all kinds of
possibilities through which that character

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.450
could return from the dead.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.560
But how exactly will Carrie-Anne Moss return
as Trinity?

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.541
Her character is quite clearly dead after
being impaled on machinery at the end of The

00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:22.130
Matrix Revolutions.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.840
She's an amazing warrior, but she's not The
One.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.229
Thankfully, the sci-fi realm of this franchise
offers plenty of possibilities for her return

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:30.420
as well.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.770
Humans aren't born so much as they're grown,
which leaves the door open for genetic engineering,

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.119
cloning, and all manner of other things.

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:39.060
Perhaps Trinity was replicated.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.240
There's also the possibility that Trinity
now only exists as software, a program within

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.850
the Matrix conceived to replace her physical
self, made from preserved data about her personality

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.979
and appearance.

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:53.200
However it happens, her return could ultimately
be even more fascinating than Neo's.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.800
While Neo and Trinity journey to the Machine
City to put an end to the war in The Matrix

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:02.590
Revolutions, Morpheus stays behind to help
with the final battle at Zion, arriving at

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:06.919
the last minute so Link could activate an
EMP that effectively pauses the battle so

00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:09.200
the humans can prepare for their last stand.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.510
When Neo reaches a truce with the Machines,
Morpheus is among the survivors of Zion, one

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.060
of the last surviving leaders of the free
human race.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.870
Laurence Fishburne, who played Morpheus in
the original Matrix trilogy, was notably absent

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.430
from the list of names attached to the new
film.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.970
That doesn't necessarily mean he won't be
in the movie, but in the event Fishburne's

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.750
not around, then what happened to Morpheus?

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.370
Does the story just not concern him?

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.450
Will he be played by a different actor?

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:37.070
He's too big of a presence in the franchise
for the film to ignore, so we can't wait to

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:40.840
see how The Matrix 4 explains what happened
to everybody's favorite freedom fighter.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:46.530
The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix Revolutions
established that the Matrix is full of rogue

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.820
programs.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.530
Some of these are from much older versions
of the Matrix, and they have their own agendas,

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.980
plans, and seemingly supernatural abilities.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.682
The Oracle tells Neo that these are the source
of humanity's stories about vampires, werewolves,

00:02:57.682 --> 00:03:03.840
and other creatures, as the programs basically
do as they please after refusing deletion.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.510
When the Matrix rebooted at the end of Revolutions,
we saw that both the Oracle and the Architect

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:11.950
were still present, but what about the rogue
programs?

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:15.790
Is the Merovingian still scheming within the
next version of the simulation?

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.040
Is the Trainman?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.180
What other rogue programs might have resisted
deletion the last time around and are operating

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.180
now?

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.290
It'll be very interesting indeed to see the
state of rogue programs in the new version

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.280
of this world.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:31.840
In The Matrix Reloaded, Neo meets a character
called Seraph, a program serving and protecting

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:32.860
the Oracle.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.840
The guy acts as an authenticator for visitors
by fighting them before they can see her.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.990
It's eventually made clear that Seraph is
unusual, even by the standards of other programs

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.160
with strange abilities.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.510
When Neo looks at him through the Matrix's
code, he sees a golden, burning light while

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.400
everything else around Seraph is green.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.150
At one point, one of the Merovingian's thugs
refers to him as "wingless."

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:56.730
In the multiplayer game The Matrix Online,
it's revealed that Seraph once acted as an

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.060
agent in the first version of the Matrix,
the "paradise" version, making him something

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.760
akin to an angel.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.340
Seraph's "angel" status makes him apparently
second only to Neo in terms of fighting ability,

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.210
and his status as a product of the first Matrix
makes him one of the oldest programs in existence.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.190
So will he show up in The Matrix 4?

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.669
He's a fascinating character, and it would
be great to see the next film return to him

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.800
as a key part of the mythos.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:24.200
At the end of Revolutions, Neo manages to
negotiate a peace between the Machines and

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.270
the humans.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:29.039
Human civilization would be allowed to continue
in some form, and humans would have a chance

00:04:29.039 --> 00:04:30.979
to leave the Matrix upfront.

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:33.610
So what does human civilization look like
now?

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.110
it'll be interesting to see what's changed.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.870
Is Zion still the only human city?

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:41.710
Have humans found a way to survive on the
surface with the Machines' heavy pollution?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:42.710
Are there more people?

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:46.460
The biggest question is whether the peace
lasted, and if so, for how long?

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:50.449
"Just how long do you think this peace is
going to last?"

00:04:50.449 --> 00:04:54.309
"As long as it can."

00:04:54.309 --> 00:04:58.569
The Architect took a cynical view of things,
so it's quite possible that he began at that

00:04:58.569 --> 00:05:03.800
very moment to explore new ways to subjugate
and undermine humanity's future as supposedly

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.800
free.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.169
And since so much of the thematic weight of
The Matrix is already tied up in themes of

00:05:08.169 --> 00:05:12.789
determinism versus free will, it's easy to
see how that cycle would begin again.

00:05:12.789 --> 00:05:16.909
It's also possible that humans have used their
newfound ability to leave the Matrix and begin

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:21.040
a kind of cold war with the Machines, with
the hope of wiping them out entirely.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:25.480
If you're the type of fan who likes to pick
apart the world established in The Matrix,

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:29.960
you may have arrived at a lingering question:
Why wouldn't the Machines have adopted alternative

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.259
means of energy rather than just farming humans?

00:05:33.259 --> 00:05:36.949
After the peace established in The Matrix
Revolutions, it's a question that has to come

00:05:36.949 --> 00:05:37.949
up again.

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:41.809
With humans now granted the freedom to choose
to leave the Matrix or not as the result of

00:05:41.809 --> 00:05:45.969
Neo's sacrifice, how have the Machines adapted
to their new co-existence?

00:05:45.969 --> 00:05:48.169
Have they adopted alternative means of energy?

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:52.229
If humanity changed, then the Machines likely
had to do some kind of adjusting as well,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.040
and that will be quite an interesting idea
for The Matrix 4 to explore.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:00.520
Where Neo had to be dragged out of the Matrix
after some convincing by Morpheus, humans

00:06:00.539 --> 00:06:02.779
will now be given an upfront decision.

00:06:02.779 --> 00:06:06.689
They can leave the simulated universe they
know for a free and real life in a harsher

00:06:06.689 --> 00:06:10.680
world, or they can stay in the Matrix with
all its simulated modern comfort.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.360
"Ohhhh.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.099
Ignorance is bliss."

00:06:15.099 --> 00:06:18.620
As the original trilogy made clear, there
were some who will choose to forget about

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:22.920
the real world and simply carry on living
in the Matrix, with modern conveniences, while

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.800
others will choose reality.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:28.099
Now that everyone gets to make that choice,
the big question is what will that choice

00:06:28.099 --> 00:06:29.150
look like?

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:30.759
How do the Machines present their argument?

00:06:30.759 --> 00:06:34.439
Do both sides try to convince souls in the
Matrix to stay or go?

00:06:34.439 --> 00:06:37.979
If you're born outside the Matrix, can you
try it and see if you'd like to stay?

00:06:37.979 --> 00:06:42.370
The film reportedly starts production in early
2020, so maybe it won't be too long before

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.009
we find out.

